From 5df1e1a0f65893ca28843e144a257f174b2ae49b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qr0n <77075118+qr0n@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 04:33:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 18/18] CUDA: GP100: gated delta-net prefill at 4 state columns
 per warp; Q3_K output-sized matrices at 8 rows per warp

GDN: a 2048-token prefill launched 768 blocks (24 heads x 32 column groups),
two waves at 10 blocks per SM. Four state columns per warp share the k/q loads
and l2 norms and fit one wave; every column's arithmetic is unchanged, so the
output is bit-identical. Applies to every gather variant. GP100_GDN_CPW=1
restores the stock launch (2 and 4 are accepted; 4 is the default, 8 measured
the same).

Q3_K: an output-sized matrix (Qwen3.8-27B's MTP draft head, 124160 rows,
K 2560 per card) ran ~136 GB/s at 4 rows per warp; it now takes 8, the rule
the Q6_K output head already uses.

2x P100, -sm tensor, Qwen3.8-27B UD-Q4_K_XL, alternating cooled A/B, 0%
thermal throttle: pp2048 446.7 -> 463.8 (+3.8%), pp8192 436.7 -> 453.2
(+3.8%), pp512 239.1 -> 244.1 (+2.1%); real prompts of 4-11k tokens +3.4..3.7%
prefill; MTP decode 44.9 -> 45.4 tok/s (+1.2%); plain decode unchanged.
test-backend-ops MUL_MAT and GATED_DELTA_NET pass; KLD vs a Q8_0 reference at
-ub 1 / 5 / 512 identical to before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
